    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T17:00:44Z",
    "body": "Review addressed in d1c73221:\n\n1. **Blocker (Fanuc vs check on a -X table):** `fanuc.cps` now refuses, by name, a tilt on a lone rotary stated along -X: `tilted move on rotary A, stated along -X - this dialect posts the stream's angle unnegated, so it would leave the travel the machine check judged`. It uses the same \"exactly one rotary, along X\" test the check uses (`x² ≥ 0.998·|d|²`). I chose refusing over applying the sign in the post, because negating would quietly change G43.4 output for a direction no shipped machine states. No shipped machine states `[-1,0,0]`, so no shipped output changes. Pinned by `fourth_axis_pose::the_fanuc_dialect_refuses_a_lone_a_stated_along_minus_x`: on a `[-1,0,0]` 0..90 table, A-45 is refused and no `A-45` is written; on `[1,0,0]` it posts as before.\n2. **Doc claim:** `judge.rs` now says only the PathPilot post agrees pose-for-pose, and that the Fanuc dialect refuses the B of A0 B180 and the -X table by name.\n\nNon-blocking notes: whether a refused Fanuc tilt should block the post (rather than drop the move with a warning), and the Doosan DNM path. Both are recorded as open in the decision file and the PR body; that's a maintainer call.\n\nGate on d1c73221, run alone: fourth_axis_pose 6/6, fanuc_post 11/11, machine 33/33, tormach_fourth_axis 12/12, microarc_test_part 2/2, conformance 6/6, index_swing 9/9; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Ready for a re-review (at the high tier, per the safety floor).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
