    "body": "Delta review addressed in 693b2809, then merged with upstream main at 7a7dba04 (only `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` conflicted; took main's 14):\n\n1. **Doosan (blocker):** this went further than the review traced. The shipped DNM's A about X leans off Z, so the mirror sets `machine.rtcp`, and Doosan's RTCP path writes the stream's letters raw. That means it was also going to post the A0 B180 the check now passes as a **`B180` word to a machine with no B**, not only the unnegated A on a -X table. `doosan-dnm.cps` now refuses both by name (`missingLetter` and the -X check, the same as fanuc.cps). Pinned by `the_doosan_dialect_refuses_a_b_on_its_a_only_table` (shipped DNM: the check passes, the post refuses B and writes no `B180`) and `the_doosan_dialect_refuses_a_turning_a_stated_along_minus_x`. Both fail against the previous `doosan-dnm.cps`. They live in `fourth_axis_pose.rs`, because `doosan_dnm_post.rs` (353 lines) would pass 400.\n2. **judge.rs wording:** now names both G43.4 dialects (Fanuc, Doosan): they write letters unnegated and refuse those two cases by name.\n3. **A0 over-refusal (your note):** fixed in both posts. Only a non-zero A is refused on the -X table, since A0 is the same word on either sign. Pinned by `an_upright_a0_still_posts_on_a_minus_x_fanuc_table` and the upright run in the Doosan -X test.\n\nDropped cuts: thanks for checking the app path. The decision file now records that a refused tilt blocks the post in the app, and leaves the dev CLI question to the maintainer.\n\nGate on 7a7dba04: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (482 passed, 0 failed); run alone, fourth_axis_pose 9/9, doosan_dnm_post 7/7, fanuc_post 11/11, machine 33/33, tormach_fourth_axis 12/12, microarc_test_part 2/2, conformance 6/6, index_swing 9/9; clippy -p camcraft-app clean. Ready for a re-review, at the high tier per the safety floor.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
